WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:10.200
Hey guys, now most of you know the&nbsp;
amazing story of David and Goliath.&nbsp;

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.120
I mean, you hear it everywhere,&nbsp;
because it inspires people to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:21.720
also overcome the challenges in their lives.
And I mean, who cannot be inspired by David,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:29.960
an underdog who everybody thought&nbsp;
would not be able to defeat Goliath.&nbsp;

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:34.280
A shepherd's boy, he came and did it&nbsp;
when everyone in Israel was afraid.&nbsp;

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.160
I mean, they had fierce warriors -&nbsp;
strong guys - but they were afraid.&nbsp;

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.160
And then here comes David.&nbsp;

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.080
Fearless.
Think about this.&nbsp;

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.520
Even his own father did&nbsp;
not include David at first.&nbsp;

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.680
When he let all his other&nbsp;
sons stand in front of Samuel.&nbsp;

00:00:53.680 --> 00:01:00.400
When Samuel would choose the new king&nbsp;
from Jesse's sons. Listen to this.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.760
[1 Samuel 16:10-12]

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.000
So here, God chose David to become&nbsp;
the king of Israel, the future king.&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.280
But Saul was still king.
And in this time the army&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:58.320
of the Philistines, they came to have war&nbsp;
with Israel, and with them, came a champion.&nbsp;

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:02.920
Their champion, the giant Goliath.
And this is what happened.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.400
[1 Samuel 17:3-4]

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.400
Now how tall is that?
That's around 9 feet and 10 inches.&nbsp;

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.000
That's around 3 meters.
That's huge.&nbsp;

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.320
Imagine you stand in front of a mountain.
Man, giant, 3 meters tall.&nbsp;

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.120
He wasn't just tall but he was he was very strong.
I'll get to that in a minute.&nbsp;

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.120
I want to mention something interesting here.
He was probably from the tribe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:50.400
from the people of the Anakim.
If you watch my video on the Nephilim, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.200
mighty man of all the giants, you would know this.
But if you haven't, go check it out.&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:01.480
It's a very interesting series that I'm covering.
We also know that Goliath had brothers - other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:05.240
giants - and here's the thing.
Today you have a lot of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:11.440
who who grow tall and there are medical problems&nbsp;
you know and usually they're not always strong.&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.420
But these giants were strong.
Listen to this:

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.040
[1 Samuel 17:5-7]

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:48.880
His bronze armor alone was 125&nbsp;
pounds... 56 kilograms ... that's heavy.&nbsp;

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.480
I mean, you can try to put it on and&nbsp;
just walk a little bit but put that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.960
on ... walk for miles towards an enemy...&nbsp;
and then have the energy to still taunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:01.340
them and ready for a battle.
You won't be able to do that.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.640
[1 Samuel 17:8-11]

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:57.760
So this probably wasn't just a normal giant even.
This guy was fierce, almost looked like he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:04.440
blood in his eyes, ready just to to kill&nbsp;
and devour these little men, like straw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:08.200
because the whole of Israel,&nbsp;
they were afraid of this giant.&nbsp;

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.040
I mean, they must have had&nbsp;
powerful champions as well.&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:17.760
Strong men but even they were afraid&nbsp;
at Goliath because Verse 24 says:

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.040
[1 Samuel 17:24]

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:34.560
Now you know what happened next ... David&nbsp;
without fear came against Goliath and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.440
know how that ended for him. But there's&nbsp;
a lot of things that people don't know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.040
about the story or that they miss&nbsp;
and I want to share that with you.&nbsp;

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:46.680
But before I explain that to you, you&nbsp;
need to understand something else first.&nbsp;

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:53.600
And that is that this was not just a battle&nbsp;
between a man and a giant - between Israel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:06:00.440
and the Philistines - this was a battle between&nbsp;
good and evil, the battle that all men and women&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.440
face in their lives.
Listen to this:

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.400
[1 Samuel 17:42-43]

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:29.240
So Goliath cursed him with his gods,&nbsp;
and this is important because we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:36.360
know that these gods were demons.
Remember Deuteronomy 32:17 says ...

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:47.160
Paul also says in 1 Corinthians 10:19-20:

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:13.960
Go watch the series that I started on the&nbsp;
truths that all men need to know about life.&nbsp;

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:20.320
In that video series I explain my experience with&nbsp;
demons growing up and after that, also the history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:25.360
of how men started to worship demons thinking&nbsp;
they are gods and how religion started before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.320
the flood and after the flood.
Now, let's move forward.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:31.400
[1 Samuel 17:44-45]

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:58.440
You see, David did not fight through&nbsp;
the flesh with his own power.&nbsp;

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:03.360
He fought with God's power that&nbsp;
was in him, through the Spirit.&nbsp;

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.560
You see, he did not have self-confidence.&nbsp;

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:10.560
He had God confidence.
He said in Verse 46:

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:53.480
You see, David had no fear.
He knew God was with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:56.680
that God's spirit is on him, guiding his own will.&nbsp;

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:03.480
His own emotions, his own intellect, his soul.
You know, that's the difference.&nbsp;

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.800
We talked about this on my channel a lot,&nbsp;
between self-confidence and God- confidence.&nbsp;

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:14.800
Now David knew that God's spirit is on him giving&nbsp;
him the strength and that is why he had no fear.&nbsp;

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.520
How do we know this?
How do we know this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:25.120
that David acted through the spirit?
It happened back when Samuel anointed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:28.680
David to be king.
Listen to this:

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:31.760
[1 Samuel 16:13]

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:50.400
Now, this is amazing, because not only did&nbsp;
David act through the power of the Holy Spirit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:59.120
not only that, but he ran towards Goliath.
Towards the thing God wanted him to face.&nbsp;

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:03.080
This is amazing.
Normal men, even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:10.680
the most powerful men in the army of Israel,&nbsp;
they looked at Goliath and they were afraid.&nbsp;

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:19.800
David had no fear because of God's Spirit in him.
Not only that, but he he ran towards him to fight.&nbsp;

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:26.960
How many times have you buckled because of fear?
The challenges, the obstacles, the problems in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:33.360
your own life? How many times have you buckled&nbsp;
out of fear because you acted in your flesh and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:38.120
not through the power of the Spirit?
God's spirit that is in you.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.520
Verse 48 says:

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:54.280
Most people miss this.
Without fear, because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:59.600
was in the Spirit, acting in the&nbsp;
Spirit, he ran towards his enemy.&nbsp;

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.760
To face him.
Quickly.&nbsp;

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:07.760
Fearless.
Man, how amazing is our God.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.200
Verse 49:

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:58.080
Wow, this is amazing.
You know, you might not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:03.880
face a giant Philistine, but you will&nbsp;
face many challenges in your life.&nbsp;

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:07.240
Many obstacles.
And you cannot run from it.&nbsp;

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:11.640
Neither can you fear it.
You cannot face it through your own power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:16.400
through the flesh. You need to face it with&nbsp;
the power of the Holy Spirit who is in you.&nbsp;

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:22.040
If you are a real child of God.
So many people run away from their problems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:30.760
their challenges, their giants, because of fear&nbsp;
and this is important to understand because if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:36.200
do that, those problems will just stay there.
Those challenges will stay there.&nbsp;

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:42.240
Not only that, they might grow, and there&nbsp;
will be more problems that's added to it.&nbsp;

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:49.120
So later on in life you'll just be carrying&nbsp;
a heavy heavy load so big that you'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:53.120
buckle under the pressure.
You need to handle your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:58.840
giants the moment they surface.
David also said in Psalm 56:3:

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:22.600
The moment you fear, you need to understand that&nbsp;
that is the moment that you're not trusting God.&nbsp;

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:28.840
That's when you are starting to act in the flesh&nbsp;
through your own power and not in the Spirit.&nbsp;

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:34.480
And you have no excuses because today&nbsp;
since 2,000 years ago after Jesus Christ,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:41.200
all reborn believers, when we accept Jesus&nbsp;
Christ as our Lord and Savior, He gives us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:52.440
His Spirit so you have the Spirit of God in you to&nbsp;
help you to overcome any challenge in your life.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:54.440
[Acts 2:38]

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.880
And listen to this:

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:15.120
And you will - not maybe - not probably -&nbsp;
you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.&nbsp;

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.800
You need to understand this.
When you are declared righteous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:23.320
when you come to repentance, when you truly accept&nbsp;
Jesus Christ as Lord and Savior, when He makes you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:29.640
a new creation, He gives you His Spirit.
You are sealed by the Spirit.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.600
[Ephesians 1:13]

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:47.600
So how do you do this?
How do you overcome challenges in your life?&nbsp;

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:51.000
You need to be weak.
Weak in yourself to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:59.560
such a degree where you deny yourself, your own&nbsp;
selfish desires, your own self-determining will.&nbsp;

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:06.680
It needs to be under the power of God.
He needs to sit on your throne, not you.&nbsp;

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:11.040
It is only when you come to the end of&nbsp;
yourself - your own power - oh me me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:18.880
me - it is only when you come to the end of that&nbsp;
life where you surrender to the power of God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:24.280
where He can start to work through you.
Let me tell you when you do that, when you let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:29.800
the Holy Spirit work through you and guide your&nbsp;
soul out there in the world, everything you do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:36.640
everything you say, everything you do.
Then, nothing will be impossible for you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:40.960
to accomplish God's plan and purpose for&nbsp;
your life, because He will give you what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:43.840
you need to accomplish it.
And He will give you the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:51.880
power through the Holy Spirit that is in you.
And the Spirit of God who is in you is not afraid.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.320
[2 Timothy 1:7]

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:10.960
Satan, on the other hand, he uses&nbsp;
a spirit of fear and uncertainty.&nbsp;

